# Accessibility & UX — Quantia Web

Baseline: WCAG 2.1 AA and Resolución 1519 de 2020 (MinTIC), because Quantia is used in a public
university context. Target: axe with zero violations and Lighthouse Accessibility ≥ 95 on every route.
These are build rules, not a review checklist: apply them while writing code.

## 1. Perceivable
- Contrast ≥ 4.5:1 for normal text; ≥ 3:1 for large text (≥ 24 px, or ≥ 18.66 px bold), icons,
  control borders and focus rings. Check BOTH themes. Never lower opacity to "soften" text.
- Color is NEVER the only carrier of meaning. Every status combines color + text + icon/shape.
  One single source of truth, consumed by `Badge`, `AlertList`, `TaskRow`, `ProjectCard`:

| `ProjectStatus` (contract) | Spanish label | Tone token | Icon shape |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `FORMULATION` | En formulación | `theme.colors.text.secondary` (neutral) | Pencil |
| `ACTIVE` | En curso | `theme.colors.status.info` | Clock |
| `DELAYED` | Retrasado | `theme.colors.status.danger` | Warning triangle |
| `COMPLETED` | Finalizado | `theme.colors.status.success` | Check circle |
| `CANCELLED` | Cancelado | `theme.colors.text.secondary` (neutral) | Crossed circle |

| `TaskStatus` (contract) | Spanish label | Tone token | Icon shape |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `TODO` | Por hacer | `theme.colors.text.secondary` (neutral) | Empty circle |
| `IN_PROGRESS` | En curso | `theme.colors.status.info` | Clock |
| `BLOCKED` | Bloqueada | `theme.colors.status.warning` | Pause |
| `DONE` | Hecha | `theme.colors.status.success` | Check circle |

  Alert severity follows the same rule: Crítico (danger) · Atención (warning) · Al día (success).

~~~ts
// src/components/base/Badge/statusPresentation.ts — the ONLY place that maps status → UI
// Keys are the contract enums from @quantia/contracts; never lowercase or rename them.
export const PROJECT_STATUS_PRESENTATION = {
  FORMULATION: { label: 'En formulación', tone: 'neutral', icon: 'pencil' },
  ACTIVE:      { label: 'En curso',       tone: 'info',    icon: 'clock' },
  DELAYED:     { label: 'Retrasado',      tone: 'danger',  icon: 'warning' },
  COMPLETED:   { label: 'Finalizado',     tone: 'success', icon: 'check' },
  CANCELLED:   { label: 'Cancelado',      tone: 'neutral', icon: 'x-circle' },
} as const satisfies Record<ProjectStatus, StatusPresentation>;

export const TASK_STATUS_PRESENTATION = {
  TODO:        { label: 'Por hacer', tone: 'neutral', icon: 'circle' },
  IN_PROGRESS: { label: 'En curso',  tone: 'info',    icon: 'clock' },
  BLOCKED:     { label: 'Bloqueada', tone: 'warning', icon: 'pause' },
  DONE:        { label: 'Hecha',     tone: 'success', icon: 'check' },
} as const satisfies Record<TaskStatus, StatusPresentation>;
// Icons are decorative (aria-hidden="true"); the visible label carries the meaning.
~~~

- Typography: body `theme.typography.bodyMedium` (16 px, line-height 1.5). Labels, errors, buttons
  and table cells ≥ 14 px. The 12 px `caption` is only for supplementary metadata, never for
  labels, errors or anything actionable.
- Text must survive 200% zoom and reflow at 320 CSS px without loss or page-level horizontal scroll.
- Touch targets ≥ 44×44 px (IconButton, checkboxes, table row actions, pagination), with spacing
  tokens between adjacent targets. Mobile matters: Investigadores register progress in the field.
- Images and icons that convey information have a Spanish text alternative; decorative ones use
  `aria-hidden="true"` / `alt=""`.

## 2. Operable — keyboard and focus
- Everything works with the keyboard alone: progress form, filters, tables, tabs, menus, modals,
  date pickers, file upload. No hover-only content or actions; tooltips also open on focus.
- Visible focus always: the `focusRing` mixin (2 px, contrast ≥ 3:1) on every interactive element.
  Never `outline: none` without the ring. Never style `:focus` in a way that hides `:focus-visible`.
- Skip link as the first focusable element in `src/app/layout.tsx`: "Saltar al contenido principal"
  → `<main id="main-content" tabIndex={-1}>`.
- Tab order follows the DOM and the visual order. No positive `tabIndex`. Do not reorder visually
  with CSS what the DOM orders differently.
- Modals, side panels ("Registrar avance") and menus use Radix primitives: focus trap, `Esc` closes,
  focus returns to the trigger. Never hand-roll a modal.
- Use native elements first (`button`, `a`, `input`, `select`). A clickable `div` is forbidden.
- Do not trap focus outside overlays; do not auto-move focus except on route change (to the page
  `h1`), on submit errors (to the first invalid field) and when opening/closing overlays.

## 3. Understandable — forms, errors and language
- `<html lang="es-CO">`. All UI copy in Spanish.
- Persistent visible labels (`<label htmlFor>`) for every field. A placeholder is never the label;
  it may only show an example ("Ej.: 15/10/2026"). Required fields say "(obligatorio)" in text.
- Errors are text next to the field, linked with `aria-describedby` + `aria-invalid="true"`, and say
  how to fix it ("Ingresa una fecha con formato DD/MM/AAAA"). Never only a red border or a toast.
  On submit with errors: focus the first invalid field (and show a summary on long forms).
- Domain language, never system language. Never show raw status codes, enum values or stack traces:

| Write | Never write |
| --- | --- |
| Registrar avance | Crear registro en bitácora |
| Sincronizando con Notion | sync_status=pending |
| No tienes permiso para ver esta sección | 403 Forbidden |
| Tu sesión expiró. Inicia sesión de nuevo | JWT expired / 401 |
| Generar reporte | Crear job / encolar |
| Reintentar sincronización | Re-enqueue |
| Estamos procesando demasiadas solicitudes | 429 Too Many Requests |

- Destructive actions use `ConfirmDialog` with a specific verb ("Eliminar documento"), never "Aceptar".

## 4. Formats — always through `src/lib/format`
Components never call `Intl`, `toFixed`, `toLocaleString` or date libraries directly.

| Helper | Input | Output |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `formatCOP(value)` | decimal string from the API (`"1250000.00"`) or number | `$ 1.250.000` — es-CO, thousands separators, no decimals |
| `formatDate(value, { withTime? })` | ISO string or Date | `09/10/2026` (`DD/MM/AAAA`), `09/10/2026 14:30` with time; zone America/Bogota |
| `formatPercent(value)` | number 0–100 | `45,6 %` — max 1 decimal, es-CO separator |
| `toApiDate(value)` | `DD/MM/AAAA` input or Date | ISO UTC built from 00:00 America/Bogota (date-only fields sent to the API) |

- Empty or invalid input returns "—" (never `NaN`, `Invalid Date` or `undefined`).
- Money stays a decimal string end to end: `formatCOP` only parses it to display; never add amounts as numbers.
- Inputs for money, dates and percentages accept and display the same formats.

## 5. Charts and tables
- Recharts: every chart shows value labels (`LabelList`) and a legend in text; series are
  distinguishable without color (labels, patterns or markers). Use theme tokens for colors.
- Every chart is wrapped in `<figure>` with a Spanish `<figcaption>` that states the takeaway
  ("3 proyectos con ejecución mayor al avance"), and offers "Ver como tabla" rendering an
  equivalent `DataTable`. Interpreted relations are shown as alerts, not as two numbers to compare.
- Tables are semantic: `<table>`, `<caption>`, `<th scope="col|row">`, `aria-sort` on sortable headers.
- Wide tables scroll INSIDE their container; the page never scrolls horizontally:

~~~tsx
<TableScroll role="region" aria-label="Proyectos de la convocatoria" tabIndex={0}>
  <table>…</table>
</TableScroll>
// TableScroll.styles.ts → overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; focusRing on :focus-visible
~~~

- Empty tables render `EmptyState` with a specific message and next action
  ("Sin proyectos en esta convocatoria · Cambiar filtros"), never a blank table.

## 6. Live updates, loading and motion
- D-07: real-time events NEVER reorder, insert above or move content under the cursor or the focus.
  Update the row in place and highlight it 1–2 s. If an event would change the order, keep the
  current order and show "Hay actualizaciones · Actualizar" for the user to apply them.
- Announce changes through a single polite live region (`aria-live="polite"`); use
  `role="alert"` only for blocking errors (session expired, sync failed for an Administrador).
  Never move focus because of an incoming event.
- Loading: `Skeleton` with the final structure; the container gets `aria-busy="true"` and a
  visually hidden "Cargando…". No full-page spinners; never block global navigation.
- Motion: 150/200/250 ms tokens, `transform`/`opacity` only, nothing essential conveyed only by
  animation. Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, disable shimmer, slides and highlight motion
  (keep a static highlight).
- `ConnectionStatus` banner when the socket drops: "Datos posiblemente desactualizados" + "Reconectar".

## 7. Semantics and structure
- Landmarks: `header`, `nav` (RoleSidebar, with `aria-label`), `main`, `footer`. One `h1` per page;
  headings in order (`h1` → `h2` → `h3`), never chosen for size.
- ARIA only when native HTML is not enough; never contradict native semantics.
- Radix provides the accessible base; Shadcn is a pattern reference only.
- Keep `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y` errors at zero; never disable its rules inline.

## 8. Critical DON'Ts
- Do NOT convey status by color alone or use red/amber/green without label and icon.
- Do NOT remove `:focus-visible`, use positive `tabIndex` or clickable `div`/`span`.
- Do NOT use placeholders as labels or show errors only with color or toasts.
- Do NOT format money, dates or percentages outside `formatCOP`, `formatDate`, `formatPercent`.
- Do NOT render a chart without value labels and a table equivalent.
- Do NOT let any route scroll horizontally at 390 px (or 320 px reflow).
- Do NOT reorder lists or steal focus on real-time events.
- Do NOT show technical messages, codes or enum values to users.

## 9. Verification before saying it is done
1. axe: zero violations on every touched route, in all states (loading, empty, error, 403) and both themes.
2. Lighthouse Accessibility ≥ 95 on every touched route.
3. Keyboard-only walkthrough of the flow: skip link, tab order, focus visible, `Esc` closes overlays,
   focus returns to the trigger.
4. Screen reader smoke test (NVDA or VoiceOver) on F-01, F-02 or F-03 when the change touches them.
5. 390 / 768 / 1280 px with no page-level horizontal scroll; 200% zoom readable.
6. `prefers-reduced-motion` emulated: no essential animation, no shimmer.
7. Statuses show color + text + icon; formats come from `src/lib/format`.

